WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:02.700
Pamyun!

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.840
We now present Shirobaco Reading Theater!

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.840
If you don't all enjoy it to the very last moment,

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.840
you'll make poor widdle Sakurako cry!

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.940
"'The Legend That Could Not Become Legend'

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.940
The Story of 12,000 Years Ago"

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.780
"To Battle! With My Existence on the Line"

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.880
12,000 years ago.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:23.350
In an era when civilization did not yet exist.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.190
People touched the laws of truth,

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.590
and possessed the power to materialize their feelings.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.400
By drawing power from the world of truth,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.100
they could make the rain fall by saying the word rain,

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.870
could make the wind blow by whispering the word wind.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.040
If it were the right time and right place.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.710
However, they had no means to record those feelings or deliver them far away.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:55.950
In order to do that, they invented writing.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.960
Humans, having gained the ability of transmission through writing,

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.290
developed their civilization at a rapid pace.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.800
However, there was one tribe who saw a danger in this.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.100
I warn you,

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:14.440
there will come a day when writing will bring harm to humanity!

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.440
Writing, which carries lies as easily as truth, will run rampant.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.310
Surely, all that can lie ahead is a pitiful future for humans, bereft of dignity.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.920
This is precisely why we must push for the abolition of writing!

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.620
They were the Truth Tribe, who held that the most precious thing of all

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:35.320
was our ability to connect with the world of truth.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:43.600
They feared that overreliance on writing would weaken that power.

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:49.770
However, humans will not so easily let go of a convenient thing.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.770
What pitiful future?

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.780
Writing is necessary for the advance of civilization!

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:57.850
Those people who interfere with societal progress are evil!

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:00.450
We won't let you abolish writing!

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.450
Let's protect our writing!

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:06.020
Yes, in the name of our prosperous future!

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.490
And so, the Writing Tribe and
Truth Tribe came into conflict,

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:14.130
ultimately leading to a great war.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:17.630
The Writing Tribe held an overwhelming numerical advantage.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:24.170
However, the ones who first took the upper hand were the Truth Tribe.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:26.880
By contacting the world of truth,

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.980
they brought forth a warped power not of this world,

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.880
the destroying angels.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:39.320
As their name would suggest, the angels committed terrible massacres.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.360
Never doubting their own justice,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.030
the war raged on because neither side could tolerate the other's position.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:49.000
In the name of all humanity, writing will be abolished!

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.400
Any who oppose this will be eliminated!

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.210
However, even in the depths of despair,

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:59.730
there was one youth who never abandoned hope.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.090
What?

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:17.050
What folly! You think you can stand against us?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.890
Why have you not killed me?

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.300
To fear is to have a heart.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.640
And those with a heart, I will not kill.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.600
For I am...

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.230
...a just person!

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:11.580
That was the meeting between the girl of the Truth Tribe, Nesta,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.310
and the young man of the Writing Tribe, Kiryu.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.320
What was that man?

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:22.930
Why did he not slay me, his enemy?

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.630
I don't understand...

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.690
I want to know more! About him!

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.100
I don't think of you as an enemy.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.600
I met that man again.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:38.610
He said he does not wish to fight me.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:41.310
What goes through his mind?

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:45.110
Both writing and feelings are important.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:47.950
I'm sure you and I can come to understand one another.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.320
Today, I met him once more.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.460
Why is it? My chest always tightens when I hear him speak.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:57.960
I want to learn more of him!

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.630
You are too pure.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:05.300
That is why you stained your hands in blood without hesitation.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:08.840
I learned his name: Kiryu.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.810
What a lovely name. Kiryu.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:17.680
Oh, why does just speaking that name make my heart race?

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.820
Nesta. Is that your name?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.320
How strange. Being with you eases my heart.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:27.990
Kiryu! I want to know you better!

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:30.530
And I want you to know me, as well!

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.200
I want to show you every facet of myself!

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.370
I can still feel the warmth from holding you in my arms.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.340
Hold me more! With greater strength!

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:42.340
Strongly, so strongly I could break!

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:45.070
I never want to let this warmth go!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:48.180
I want to indulge greedily in your body and heart!

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.910
Oh, Kiryu! I...!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.520
Nesta, I...!

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.010
--...love you!
--...love you!

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.860
An intense love transcending tribal boundaries.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.930
This was unacceptable.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.360
In order to tear them apart,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.400
their tribes urged them many times to open their eyes.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.100
But, no matter what anyone said,

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.610
their love never wavered.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:22.080
For as long as the war drags on, no one will accept our love.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.380
In that case...

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:29.050
Let us end the fighting. With our own hands.

00:06:29.050 --> 00:06:30.720
Indeed.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.230
Let us end it. With our power. With our voices.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.790
Sousei.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.760
Gattai.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:47.070
--Awaken, Aquarion!
--Awaken, Aquarion!

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:50.570
When their combined voices reached the world of truth,

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:55.340
their hearts became one and summoned Aquarion Logos!

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.980
The power of the voice would come to be known as Verbalism.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:06.420
Logos moved to end the conflict between the two tribes.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:11.260
Even the destroying angels were unable to stop Logos.

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.470
Damn you, Aquarion Logos! You accursed thing!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:19.300
Still, I will not let it end here.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:22.600
If their voices can give power to writing,

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:26.010
I will devour that writing, concept and all!

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:30.610
In order to resist Aquarion Logos,

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.310
the Truth Tribe created a being that devoured written words' concepts.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:39.520
That was the concept-devouring Aquarion.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:45.150
Its core would later come to be known as Vector-Ga.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:52.830
Falling in battle, Nesta was taken captive by the Writing Tribe.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:58.710
Where is he?! Is Kiryu all right?!

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:02.680
Oh, Kiryu, is it? You mean that traitor?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.480
I hear he was captured by the Truth Tribe and executed.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.720
You must be lying!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.320
It's the truth.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:15.160
I hear it was a boring execution-- the head came off in a single strike.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.490
No...

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:20.500
What a pitiful man.

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:25.900
Had he not fallen for a woman like you, he needn't have died so pathetically.

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:29.370
Oh, Kiryu!

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:35.880
Here is a letter Kiryu wrote just before his execution.

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:45.590
However, having rejected writing as a member of the Truth Tribe,

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:49.090
Nesta could not read.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.230
What does it say?

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:54.100
It's packed full of his hatred and resentment towards you.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:57.590
He says he never should have loved you.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.100
It was a mistake to love her.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:05.240
That filthy woman. Because of her, I...

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:06.540
No...

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:10.050
I never should have loved her, never should have met her.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:11.780
I was wrong!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:15.780
Because of that woman who never deserved my love, I...!

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.620
No!!

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:26.060
What a piteous woman.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:30.730
As a small mercy, let us send you to be with Kiryu.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:35.230
Yes, with that accursed Aquarion Logos, as well!

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:40.910
And so, Nesta was loaded aboard Aquarion Logos

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:46.110
and was burned alive, sending her to her tragic fate.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:51.820
However, her soul, which died in despair, could not pass on to heaven.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.820
It caused a certain phenomenon to happen.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:58.630
Nesta's despair, her hatred, took form,

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:03.330
and created a gap between the real world and the world of truth.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.270
That is the Logos World.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:11.970
And so, the Truth Tribe, unable to materialize their feelings, lost power,

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:16.010
and the war ended with the Writing Tribe victorious.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:20.120
Since then, the culture of writing has advanced rapidly,

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:25.190
and writing has become essential for humans.

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:28.320
In time, the Logos World filled with written words,

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:32.490
and modern society, where words and concepts are tied together, formed.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:40.970
This is the tragic history of a man and woman toyed with by fate.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:42.370
Yes!

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:45.170
It is the legend that could not become legend.

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:58.490
<i>The world is engulfed by an unvoiced scream</i>

00:10:58.490 --> 00:11:04.390
<i>and I wait for it to reach and stir</i> <i>a certain someone's heart</i>

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:10.200
<i>With strength flowing to the edges of our souls</i>

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:16.510
<i>we set out into the white</i> <i>morning haze, without hesitation</i>

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:19.410
<i>I want to know everything about you</i>

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:29.410
<i>But just when I thought</i>
<i>I had you, you were gone</i>

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:38.530
<i>It's love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:45.100
<i>These tightly-sealed, silent lips</i>

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:49.470
<i>gently reply back in kind</i>

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:53.740
<i>And with love, affection, passion, expression</i>

00:11:53.740 --> 00:12:00.250
<i>Now, from the last of the words I couldn't find,</i>

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:08.950
<i>the music begins</i>

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:25.440
Found it! If I have this...

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.910
Just what do you plan to do?

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:29.480
I'm going home!

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:33.580
To the person who made it okay for me to live in this world!

00:12:33.580 --> 00:12:35.450
How stupid.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:40.090
No matter how strongly you feel for him, that man may have forgotten you.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.760
That's not true!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.430
People easily betray others.

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:48.330
Love is hollow and unreliable.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.800
He made me a promise.

00:12:51.800 --> 00:12:54.800
I'm going to save it! I'll become the savior!

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.100
I believe in that voice!

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:01.110
You believe? In whom?

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:02.600
Whom?

00:13:06.350 --> 00:13:10.650
Akira Kaibuki must be quite the important person to you.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.790
But feeling that way about someone

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:16.520
means pouring some of your heart into them.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:21.360
The more a person cares for him,

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:24.630
the sooner his concept will be lost from their mind.

00:13:33.180 --> 00:13:34.980
I'm going home!

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.380
Why?

00:13:36.380 --> 00:13:40.710
Why go so far for a person whose name you can't even remember?

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:45.050
Because he's important...

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:47.020
I have to go back.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:53.220
Because, even if I don't remember,
I know. I want to be at his side.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:59.500
Memories remain beautiful so long as they stay trapped in the past.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:01.700
I'm a little jealous...

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:05.540
It makes me want to kill her.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.840
Just kidding!

00:14:14.380 --> 00:14:16.280
Subete...

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:20.520
See her back to her room.

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.860
"Please refrain from

00:14:21.690 --> 00:14:24.860
taking pictures of the staff."

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.860
Akira is going to vanish?

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.190
Th-That's awful...!

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:27.700
Considering what Maia told me,

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:32.030
as well as our sudden troubles remembering Akira,

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:33.870
I'm reasonably certain that's the case.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.700
It must be because of Vector-Ga.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:38.710
I'm sorry, Akira. We've known all along that machine is dan--

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:41.540
I needed its power. I regret nothing.

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:43.750
How can you talk like that?!

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:46.920
How can you just... accept it?

00:14:46.920 --> 00:14:48.920
Are you okay with this?

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:53.050
You're planning to keep fighting with your very existence at risk?

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.620
Yeah.

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.730
I'll save the world for Maia.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.060
Because I'm the savior.

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:02.730
The source of Akira's extraordinary Verbalism ability...

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.770
I think I finally know what it is.

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:09.400
In today's world, clearly voicing your intents and feelings

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:11.240
is the more difficult choice.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:15.280
The more earnest the person, the more coldly people tend to look at them.

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:20.420
Even so, no matter what anyone said to you, you kept on voicing it.

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.920
That you were the savior.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.090
That voice, imbued with an unshakable will,

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:29.680
may have given you a bottomless reserve of Verbalism.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.760
There was the first time we met...

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.800
Right, he forcibly pulled in my Vector and Gattaied with me, and then...

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:53.710
"Gattai with Vectors

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:53.710
Tanabata, papier-mâché displays

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:53.710
Hayato Kujyo, Tsutomu Domon

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:53.710
Karan Uminagi"

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.110
Tanabata! We made papier-mâché displays together, right?

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:51.950
With Kokone Kikogami, Hayato Kujyo,
Tsutomu Domon, Karan Uminagi, and...

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.280
Why?

00:15:59.120 --> 00:16:00.820
Why?!

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.320
No...

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.540
Shizuka, why have you set another place at the table?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.640
Because it's for...

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.180
Oh, why <i>did</i> I do that?

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:23.480
"First meeting

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:23.480
Gattai with Vectors

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:23.480
Tanabata, papier-mâché displays"

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:24.150
I don't want to forget! I don't want to forget!

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:25.640
I don't want to forget!

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:33.360
"Savior"

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:35.220
For I am the savior. I'm just a savior. Savior... Savior...

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:39.230
An important word... His voice...

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:43.370
I know them! I ought to know them, but...!

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:46.900
Why can't I remember?!

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:51.370
My and Maia's memories of that moonlit night were a fabrication.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:55.210
But, still, the things Maia did for me...

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:59.080
That Maia supported me all this time. That's still true.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:01.580
Even if what started our relationship was fake,

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.550
the time I spent with Maia is no lie.

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.790
For me, these feelings are unquestionably real.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.260
Real, huh?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:19.700
As a fake relative, I think I've done pretty well.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:21.530
Wouldn't you agree?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.770
Don't take it yet, Big Brother. We're not ready.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:28.110
Wait until Subete smiles.

00:17:28.110 --> 00:17:30.780
Do we really have to take a picture?

00:17:30.780 --> 00:17:34.910
What are you saying? This is a special occasion. Of course we do!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:43.560
What are you waiting for?
Big Brother, now's your chance!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:45.120
Uh, right.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.900
Even if it means hurting Maia,

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:54.430
there is only one path left for me.

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:59.970
Akira Kaibuki, I will defeat you!

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:04.580
With my name, my existence,

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.910
my everything on the line!

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:16.660
Every word in the Logos World has begun to distort?

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.860
Is this...?

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.490
What'll happen?!

00:18:19.490 --> 00:18:23.100
By absorbing the warped words into that giant M.J.B.K.,

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.830
it makes their concepts vanish!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.340
It's even faster than with the nothingness M.J.B.K.!

00:18:27.340 --> 00:18:29.170
I'll head out right away!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.270
You can't!

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:33.640
The corrosion density of that space is off the charts!

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:37.450
If you go there in a vector, it'll warp your very existence!

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:39.110
D-Does that mean...

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.010
It's him.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.950
The kanji that represent your names may warp,

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:45.990
and you'd be absorbed into that M.J.B.K., along with your Vectors.

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:48.120
Then we can't go out there!

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.450
Move.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:56.160
That M.J.B.K. has powers gained from warping the "everything" kanji...

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.530
However, my name has already become hollow...

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.870
Verbalize.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:00.900
"Akira Kaibuki"

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:03.510
I'm reading activation signals from all vectors!

00:19:03.510 --> 00:19:05.310
Who's controlling them?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.680
We're all in here!

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:10.350
Th-The Aquariphone...!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.250
"Savior"

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:25.360
"Savior"

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.150
What is this?

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:21.860
A word...? One that was important to us...?

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:24.490
One that led us forward.

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.590
There is one. We have a friend in there!

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:30.660
We have to go!

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.760
"Voice I.D.

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.760
All Verbalism Club Staff"

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.540
It's too self-centered for you to go alone like this!

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.170
You've always been like this!

00:19:36.170 --> 00:19:38.840
No fair! You need to share!

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:40.240
Everyone...

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:44.350
B-But you're the only one who can do it! Please, win!

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:46.010
Come back in one piece!

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.520
I'm going to give you an earful when you do!

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:51.750
I'm hitting you with my Pico Hammer! Got it?

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.090
I'm sorry that every adult here was useless!

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:55.690
We're counting on you.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.190
Go!

00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:01.430
Go forth, to save what matters to you most!

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:11.870
Akira Kaibuki, heading out!

00:20:11.870 --> 00:20:15.080
I've loaded Maia Tsukigane aboard.

00:20:15.080 --> 00:20:18.880
I had to get a little forceful, but things are safer this way.

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:22.720
Once the writing in the Logos World vanishes, everything will be ready.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:26.720
Then, you just trigger the pair annihilation with Aquarion Logos.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:31.560
And modern civilization, which is made up of writing, will fall to ruin.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.960
The end is only a matter of time.

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:38.060
Do you think there's still a fool who'll challenge you even now?

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:40.800
I need there to be.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:43.300
The one who never gives up until the end--

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:47.640
the greatest true fool there ever was.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.580
Subete.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:53.780
I've always kept a professional distance with you, haven't I?

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.420
Mr. Hayashi.

00:20:57.420 --> 00:21:01.320
I know it's not my place to say this.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.810
But... do your best.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:08.930
I'm headed out.

00:21:08.930 --> 00:21:14.100
Subete!

00:21:16.470 --> 00:21:17.960
Is he here?

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:25.280
It is the alpha and the omega.
In the beginning was the word.

00:21:25.280 --> 00:21:27.950
Sousei Gattai! Worship!

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.450
Sousei Gattai! Save!

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.620
--Aquarion!
--Aquarion!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:41.190
He's here.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.620
Logos.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:51.210
Deava.

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.210
I can hear his voice!

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:55.010
Who are you?

00:21:55.010 --> 00:21:58.210
I don't know! I don't know, but...!

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:01.220
I love this voice!

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:05.550
Subete!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:08.720
I'll be taking Maia back, Subete Kenzaki!

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:11.990
It's time to settle this, Akira Kaibuki!

00:22:20.000 --> 00:22:25.770
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:22:35.850 --> 00:22:41.190
<i>With the warmth of salvation,</i>
<i>I raise my hand into the sky</i>

00:22:41.190 --> 00:22:45.930
<i>and everything in the world gains its true colors</i>

00:22:45.930 --> 00:22:48.600
<i>(Focus) A sound that was once hidden</i>

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>(on the goal) will connect us now</i>

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.200
<i>Try to understand that, okay?</i>

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.640
<i>So, are you ready?</i>

00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:59.440
<i>(heart and soul) These silent teardrops</i>

00:22:59.440 --> 00:23:02.040
<i>(narrow escape) that flow forth now</i>

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:05.550
<i>(enamored) are proof of that person's existence</i>

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:12.050
<i>You can't go inside your heart all alone</i>

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:14.620
<i>I will hesitate no more</i>

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:19.790
<i>I want to lend you a true voice</i>

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:25.000
<i>A useful life, a sparkling utopia</i>

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:34.110
<i>When your heart and voice</i> <i>tremble together, you'll surpass all</i>

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:37.510
<i>So go for your heart</i>

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:53.130
To think I'd have to rely on the kids until the very end!

00:23:53.130 --> 00:23:54.600
Maybe I should try a change of occupation...

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:57.000
The Calligraphy Class was looking for instructors.

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:00.170
When she was his secretary,
Dad lamented Sakurako's terrible writing!

00:24:00.170 --> 00:24:01.940
You're not supposed to tell people that!

00:24:01.940 --> 00:24:03.340
Writing is the window of the soul!

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:04.670
What are you trying to say?

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:06.510
Next time, Episode 25.

00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:07.980
"Episode 25: Gather! Voices for Tomorrow"

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:08.280
"Gather! Voices for Tomorrow."

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:09.770
Give me an Aquaripen!
